{
 "Start Here": {
  "A1": "WELCOME \u2014 YOUR PREMIUM WEDDING BUDGET & PAYMENT SYSTEM",
  "A2": "This is a full wedding FINANCE system, not a wedding planner \u2014 no guest list, seating chart, or day-of timeline here. It tracks every dollar: what you've budgeted, what you owe each vendor and when, who's contributed what, and what happens to your numbers if your guest count changes. Pre-loaded with a realistic sample wedding so you can see it working before you enter your own numbers \u2014 replace the sample rows on Master Budget, Vendor & Payments, and Contributions with your own.",
  "A4": "Step 0 \u2014 Go to File > Make a Copy to save this to your own Google Drive. Always work from your own copy, never the original.",
  "A6": "QUICK NAVIGATION \u2014 click a tab name to jump there",
  "A7": "\u2192 Settings",
  "A8": "\u2192 Master Budget",
  "A9": "\u2192 Vendor & Payments",
  "A10": "\u2192 Cash-Flow Timeline",
  "A11": "\u2192 Contributions",
  "A12": "\u2192 Scenario Engine",
  "A13": "\u2192 Contingency",
  "A14": "\u2192 Dashboard",
  "A15": "\u2192 Chart",
  "A17": "GET SET UP IN UNDER 5 MINUTES",
  "A18": "STEP 1: Go to Settings \u2014 enter your wedding date, target budget, estimated guest count, and contingency reserve %.",
  "A19": "STEP 2: Go to Master Budget \u2014 set a Planned Budget per category. Mark categories that scale with guest count (catering, favors, rentals) as Guest-Dependent = Y.",
  "A20": "STEP 3: Go to Vendor & Payments \u2014 add each vendor once: category, contract amount, deposit, what you've paid so far, and the next due date.",
  "A21": "That's it. Cash-Flow Timeline, Contributions reconciliation, the Scenario Engine, Contingency, and Dashboard all update automatically from what you entered in Steps 1-3 \u2014 you never re-type the same number twice.",
  "A24": "WHAT THE COLORS MEAN",
  "A25": "YELLOW",
  "B25": "YOU TYPE HERE.",
  "A26": "WHITE",
  "B26": "AUTOMATIC \u2014 calculated for you. Don't type over these; they pull from your Vendor & Payments entries.",
  "A28": "This is a planning tool, not a legal or contractual record \u2014 always keep your signed vendor contracts separately. Amounts are single-currency (your own); this tool does not perform currency conversion."
 },
